  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Kenneth B. Dart was born in Mason, Michigan, into the family behind Dart Container. After earning a mechanical-engineering degree from the University of Michigan, he joined the packaging business and rose to president. The company’s success in disposable food-service products supplied his inherited capital base. He then developed an independent investment career, including prominent positions in distressed sovereign debt and publicly traded companies.\n\nDart moved his family office to Grand Cayman and founded Dart Enterprises, building a diversified organisation around finance, property development, hospitality, retail and infrastructure. Its most visible undertaking is Camana Bay, a mixed-use waterfront community conceived on land assembled from the mid-1990s. He remains the group’s shareholder and long-term strategic investor while professional executives manage its businesses, which include commercial property and a growing portfolio of luxury hotels.",
